# Docker and Security

- Pin base images and dependencies; do not use floating production tags.
- Use multi-stage builds and copy only required runtime artifacts.
- Run as a non-root user with least privilege and a read-only filesystem where practical.
- Keep secrets out of images, manifests, logs, build arguments, and committed env files.
- Expose only required ports; keep PostgreSQL private by default.
- Set health checks, graceful shutdown, resource limits, and log rotation.
- Use separate least-privilege migration and runtime database credentials.
- Reject archive traversal, links, zip bombs, executable imports, and oversized inputs.
- Scan dependencies and images; remediate actionable high/critical findings.
- Document and test backup restoration and production-only configuration.
